-- Project file for the downstream API-boundary compile-fail probes
-- (test/api-probes/run-api-probes.sh).  It extends the canonical
-- project with the probe package, which depends on mithril-ir as an
-- ordinary external package — so hidden modules, abstract types, and
-- nominal roles are enforced exactly as any downstream consumer would
-- experience them.  The control executable must COMPILE, proving the
-- probe environment sound; the eight attack executables must FAIL to
-- compile, each for its intended boundary reason.  The probes are
-- deliberately not part of the default project, so ordinary builds
-- and tests never touch them.
import: cabal.project

packages: test/api-probes/probe

-- The probe package compiles under the repository warning policy:
-- the same warning set as the mithril-ir components plus -Werror,
-- enabled through the probe package's own werror flag exactly as the
-- imported cabal.project enables mithril-ir's.
package mithril-ir-api-probes
  flags: +werror
